{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work-list", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"facets": {}, "total-results": 533227, "items": [{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 22]], "date-time": "2026-07-22T16:40:19Z", "timestamp": 1784738419461, "version": "3.55.0"}, "publisher-location": "Stroudsburg, PA, USA", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Association for Computational Linguistics", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}, "DOI": "10.18653/v1/2025.emnlp-main.1060", "type": "proceedings-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 11, 8]], "date-time": "2025-11-08T12:29:45Z", "timestamp": 1762604985000}, "page": "20965-20980", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 1, "title": ["Tool Preferences in Agentic LLMs are Unreliable"], "prefix": "10.18653", "author": [{"given": "Kazem", "family": "Faghih", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Wenxiao", "family": "Wang", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Yize", "family": "Cheng", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Siddhant", "family": "Bharti", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Gaurang", "family": "Sriramanan", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Sriram", "family": "Balasubramanian", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Parsa", "family": "Hosseini", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Soheil", "family": "Feizi", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "1643", "event": {"name": "Proceedings of the 2025 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing", "location": "Suzhou, China", "start": {"date-parts": [[2025, 11]]}, "end": {"date-parts": [[2025, 11]]}}, "container-title": ["Proceedings of the 2025 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 11, 8]], "date-time": "2025-11-08T12:34:09Z", "timestamp": 1762605249000}, "score": 40.357185, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1060"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2025.emnlp-main.1060", "published": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 30]], "date-time": "2026-07-30T13:06:38Z", "timestamp": 1785416798438, "version": "3.56.0"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "group-title": "SSRN", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 1]], "date-time": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1767225600000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://www.uspto.gov/ip-policy/copyright-policy/copyright-basics"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>&lt;span&gt;Procedural Content Generation (PCG) provides a means of automatically&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;generating diverse, complex functional environments for video game playing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;agents. While various optimization approaches have been used to generate&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;content meeting computable functional constraints, more open-ended human priors&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;and directives are difficult to bake in to such methods. We propose Agentic&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Procedural Content Generation, a paradigm in which tool-calling large language&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;models generate video game levels that are both functional and steerable via&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;natural language. Equipped with local brushes, generative algorithms, and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;evaluation functions, agents iteratively refine content toward specified design&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;objectives. We show that the framework applies to both static level design&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;tasks and environments with dynamic gameplay mechanics, while satisfying&lt;/span&gt;\n&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;intended functional constraints. Beyond such constraints, the same framework&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;can respond to open-ended gameplay prompts and produce levels with stronger&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;structural and stylistic coherence than purely metric-driven search, suggesting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;that Agentic PCG is a framework for balancing functional constraint&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;satisfaction with free-form design control.&lt;/span&gt;</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.6499021", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 29]], "date-time": "2026-07-29T13:16:50Z", "timestamp": 1785331010000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 1, "title": ["Agentic PCG: Procedural Content Generation via Tool-using LLMs"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"given": "Zehua", "family": "Jiang", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Sam", "family": "Earle", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Ahmed", "family": "Khalifa", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Julian", "family": "Togelius", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "78", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 29]], "date-time": "2026-07-29T13:16:50Z", 